From 470dcb6d66bef44743d43468adc97dd6dfa6d414 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CVM DPDK prototype <cvm@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:47:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] app/testpmd: add authenticated CVM chunk receiver

Add a correctness-first single-queue object receiver above the synchronous
private-mbuf bridge. Authenticate fixed-size DATA chunks before committing
them to private object storage, track out-of-order delivery in a private
bitmap, and return authenticated selective ACKs through the existing TX
bridge.

Require an explicitly configured L2/L3/L4 peer and reject unsupported packet
layouts. Keep OpenSSL optional at build time and leave mlx5, the kernel module,
shared allocation, and the mbuf ABI unchanged.

